    <string name="skill_win_rate_info">How often you win a hand.\nHands won divided by hands played.\nAxis full at 40%.</string>
    <string name="skill_self_draw">Self-draw</string>
    <string name="skill_self_draw_info">How often your wins come from drawing the winning tile yourself.\nSelf-draw wins divided by hands won.\nAxis full at 50%.</string>
    <string name="skill_sub_rate">rate</string>
    <string name="skill_deal_in_rate">Deal-in rate</string>
    <string name="skill_deal_in_rate_info">How often you discard the tile that another player wins with.\nDeal-ins divided by hands played.\nA lower value is better.\nAxis full at 25%.</string>
    <string name="skill_hand_value">Hand value</string>
    <string name="skill_hand_value_info">The average points of the hands you won.\nPoints of all winning hands divided by hands won.\nAxis starts at 8 (min. hand value) and is full at 32.</string>
    <string name="skill_sub_avg">avg.</string>
    <string name="level_info">The skill score goes from 0 to 100. It is the mean of the four skills in the chart.\nEach skill gives 0 to 100 points:\n- Win rate: %1$d% or more gives 100.\n- Self-draw rate: %2$d% or more gives 100.\n- Deal-in rate: 0% gives 100 and %3$d% or more gives 0.\n- Hand value: %4$d gives 0 and %5$d or more gives 100.\nThe level follows the score. The list on the right shows the limits.\nA level needs %6$d hands. It is provisional under %7$d hands.</string>
